# Complete definition-backed domain-aspect generation in the running Drake path
#
# Dev approved the recommendation after establishing that type and domain belong
# in definitions, with a self-reference for domains and a containing-domain reference
# for their members. The work replaces line-level composition in the engine, not the
# DomainAspect schema or ownership of superDomain (which remains in DracoAspect).
#
# DomainAspectText is the target's rendered section. DomainAspectOf is the transform
# from TypeDefinition: preserve package-qualified references and all type arguments,
# take domain membership/source/target from DomainAspect, and superDomain from DracoAspect.
# The nameless anchor and missing-reference stubs retain the old emitter behavior.
# A lone source or target is preserved as authored, not validated or silently discarded.
# Member order is preserved. Text is the result and all textual target inputs.
#
# Type-parameter spelling remains an explicit Json-to-Text dependency provided by
# Drake's existing type-form renderer. This avoids a new main-to-mods dependency or
# recursion into the full emitter. The generated transform owns reference composition
# and section layout; it does not claim to replace the remaining handwritten aspects.
# Drake.emit now uses it, so the existing Emit/EmissionReceived/Emitter path does too.
# DomainLine and DomainLineOf remain available for compatibility, without claiming
# complete coverage. No user definitions or names are migrated away from those helpers.
#
# Author new types and domain memberships in drake, parse their JSON using compiled
# DrakeCLI, and generate Scala using compiled GeneratorCLI against a fresh current-
# resource overlay. All four touched definition trios passed DrakeCLI check with
# surface drift 0, json drift 0, skipped 0. The compiled tool is the previous emitter;
# this verifies definitions/round-trips, NOT the newly integrated runtime behavior.
#
# Add six tests in DomainAspectTest: complete layout, self/containment and ownership,
# parameterized references in all four positions, nameless/missing/empty-package edges,
# all corpus domain sections with no parameterized exclusion, and the running rule chain.
